  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This intimate solo performance by Mountain Goats was recorded on Saturday, September 12, 2015, at the First United Methodist Church in Ames, Iowa [1]. John performed on guitar and piano, delivering a set that includes the only archived performance of “This is My Father's World” [1][3]. The program features rare tracks such as “O Bless The Lord,” which has only two archived performances, and “Surrounded,” with fourteen archived shows [3]. “New Monster Avenue” marks a significant return, appearing for the first time in 91 archived shows after a gap of 2,738 days [3]. The setlist also includes “There Will Be No Divorce,” “Animal Mask,” “Werewolf Gimmick,” “Wild Sage,” “Maybe Sprout Wings,” “Southwestern Territory,” “Steal Smoked Fish,” “Genesis 30:3,” “Alpha Rats Nest,” “Love Love Love,” “Baboon,” “Woke Up New,” “Attention All Pickpockets,” and “Up The Wolves” [1]. An encore follows with “Dungeoneering,” the only archived performance of that song, along with “Fall of the Star High School Running Back” and “Cubs in Five” [1][3]. The recommended recording, tmg2015-09-12.radio.mp3.128, runs for 75 minutes and was taped by user AlwaysLupus [1]. It received a five-star rating from one listener who described it as their favorite recording, praising the great songs and audio quality [2]. This listener noted they used the show for work before it was removed from a previous platform, eventually finding it on archive.org [2]. The show is the 213th of 467 in the archive’s collection for the band, following a performance at Vega on September 10, 2015 [3].",
